In this paper, we consider normal factor graphs (NFGs), \ie, factor graphs where variables are associated with edges~\cite{Kschischang2001,Loeliger2004}.

The rest of this paper is structured as follows. Sections~\ref{sec:SNFG} and~\ref{sec:DENFG} introduce two types of NFGs. In particular, Section~\ref{sec:SNFG} introduces the basics of standard normal factor graphs (S-NFGs) and Section~\ref{sec:DENFG} introduces the double-edge normal factor graphs (DE-NFGs). Section~\ref{sec:GraCov} defines finite graph covers for NFGs. Sections~\ref{sec:LCT} and \ref{sec:symmetric-subspace transform} introduce the LCT and the average degree $M$-cover for both S-NFGs and DE-NFGs. Section~\ref{sec:CheckCon} presents the graph-cover theorem for a special class of DE-NFGs satisfying an easily checkable conditions.
