The following definition generalizes Definition~\ref{sec:SNFG:def:2}
from S-NFGs to DE-NFGs.

%***************************************************************************

\begin{definition}\label{sec:DENFG:def:3}
  Consider a DE-NFG $\graphN$ and let
  $\vmu $ be an SPA
  message vector\footnote{The SPA message vector $\vmu$ does
    not necessarily have to be an SPA fixed-point message vector.} for $\graphN$, as defined in~\eqref{sec:DENFG:eqn:15}. Define
    %------------------------------------------------------------------------
    \begin{align*}
        Z_{e}(\vmu)
      &\defeq
        \sum_{\txe}
            \mu_{\efi}(\txe)
            \cdot
            \mu_{\efj}(\txe), \qquad e \in \setEfull.
    \end{align*}
    %------------------------------------------------------------------------
   If $ Z_{e}(\vmu) \neq 0 $ for all $ e \in \setEfull $, then we define the $\vmu$-based Bethe partition function to be
  \begin{align}
    \ZBSPA(\graphN,\vmu)
      &\defeq \frac{\prod\limits_f Z_f(\vmu)}
        {\prod\limits_{e} Z_{e}(\vmu)},
        \label{sec:DENFG:eqn:3}
  \end{align}
  where
  \begin{align*}
    Z_f(\vmu)
    &\defeq
      \sum_{\tvx_{\setpf}}
    f\bigl( \tvx_{\setpf} \bigr)
        \cdot
        \prod_{e \in \setpf}
        \mu_{\ef}(\txe), \qquad
        f \in \setF.
  \end{align*}
  (For DE-NFGs with full and half edges, the product in the denominator on the
  right-hand side of~\eqref{sec:DENFG:eqn:3} is only over all full
  edges. Note that the expression for $\ZBSPA(\graphN,\vmu)$ is scaling
  invariant, meaning that if any of the messages in $\vmu$ is multiplied by a
  non-zero complex-valued number, then $\ZBSPA(\graphN,\vmu)$ remains unchanged.)
  The SPA-based Bethe partition function $\ZBSPA^{*}(\graphN)$ is then defined
  to be
  \begin{align*}
    \ZBSPA^{*}(\graphN)
      &\defeq \max_{\vmu}
      \ZBSPA(\graphN,\vmu),
  \end{align*}
  where the maximum is taken over all SPA fixed-point message vectors of
  $\graphN$.\footnote{Similar to the definition of the Bethe partition function in~\cite[Definition~8]{Cao2017}, for an arbitrary DE-NFG, we consider the Bethe partition function that is formulated based on the so-called pseudo-dual Bethe free energy function. Although generalizing the primal Bethe free energy function, as defined in Definition~\ref{sec:SNFG:def:1}, from S-NFGs to DE-NFGs is formally straightforward, it poses challenges because of the multi-valuedness of the complex logarithm and is left for future research.} 
  \edefinition
\end{definition}

