\begin{definition}
    \label{def:DENFG:LCT:1}

    The LCT for DE-NFG is a natural extension of the LCT for S-NFG in Definition~\ref{sec:LCT:def:1}. 
    Further definitions are made for DE-NFG.
    For each edge $ e \in \setEfull $, we apply the following changes.
    \begin{itemize}

        \item The alphabet $\set{X}_e$ is replaced by the alphabet $\tset{X}_e$, where
        $\tset{X}_e \defeq \set{X}_e \times \set{X}_e$.

        \item The special element $0 \in \set{X}_e$ is replaced by the special element
        $\tzero = (0,0) \in \tset{X}_e$. 
        (Recall that we assume $ \tzero \in \tset{X}_e $ in Definition~\ref{sec:DENFG:def:4}.)


        \item The variable $x_e \in \set{X}_e$ is replaced by the variable
        $\tx_e = (x_e,x'_e) \in \tset{X}_e$.

        \item The definition of the alphabet
        $\LCTset{X}_e \defeq \set{X}_e$ is
        replaced by the definition of the alphabet
        $\LCTtset{X}_e \defeq \tset{X}_e$.

        \item The element $0 \in \LCTset{X}_e$ is replaced by the element
        $\tzero\in \LCTtset{X}_e$.

        \item The variable $\LCT{x}_e \in \LCTset{X}_e$ is replaced by the variable
        $\LCTt{x}_e = (\LCT{x}_e, \LCT{x}'_e) \in \LCTtset{X}_{e}$.

    \end{itemize}
    The properties of the DE-NFG in Lemmas~\ref{sec:DENFG:lem:1} and~\ref{lem: nonnegative of ZBSPA for DE-NFG} imply that it is sufficient to consider the constants $\zeta_{\efj}$, $\chi_{\efj}$, $\delta_{\ef}$, and $\epsilon_{\ef}$ to be real-valued.

