\subsubsection{Repository Explorer}
The repository explorer is responsible for automatically collecting the information essential for constructing an evaluation environment for each issue. For each target repository, it autonomously extracts (1) environment dependencies from configuration files (e.g., \texttt{requirements.txt} for Python, \texttt{pom.xml} for Java); (2) the relevant test commands (such as \texttt{pytest} or \texttt{unittest} for Python, \texttt{mvn test} for Java); and (3) additional setup details from documentation files (e.g., \texttt{README.md}, \texttt{CONTRIBUTING.md}) or installation scripts. By automating this process, the Repository Explorer efficiently handles the environment diversity across different projects without manual intervention.

