\textsc{Abstract.}
    We combine energy-stable and port-Hamiltonian (\pH) systems to obtain \emph{energy-stable port-Hamiltonian (\espH) systems}. The idea is to extend the known energy-stable systems with an input--output port, which results in a \pH formulation.
    One advantage of the new \espH formulation is that it naturally preserves its \espH structure throughout discretization (in space and time) and model reduction. 
\end{quote}
