For the numerical validation of Theorem \ref{l1Square}, we persist in employing $\{C_0(x),\dots,C_{N}(x)\}$ as the orthonormal polynomial basis. For each set of $f,N,m$, we executed $500$ experiments, calculating the relative error $\frac{||f-p^\#||_2}{||f||_2}$ in the $L_2$-norm between each approximation result $p^\#$ and $f$, and considering the average value as an indicator of approximation accuracy. Guided by the numerical experiments based on the $l_1$-minimization method with the best uniform approximation error, we explore various values of $\Theta$ in Theorem \ref{l1Square}, corresponding to various upper bounds $\varepsilon=\Theta\sqrt{m}||T_N||_\infty$ on the right side of the optimization problem (\ref{Squareq}), and compared the approximation accuracy in the $L_2$-norm, as depicted in Figure \ref{fig5}.

