    This and the assumption that for all $\dm \in \N$, $\eps \in \err$, $x, p \in \R^\dm$, $a \in A$ it holds that $\norm{ t_\dm^{\pr{a}} \pr{x, p} - \pr[\big]{ \cR_\activation \pr{\ft_{\dm, \eps}^{\pr{a}} } \pr{x, p} } } \le \eps \genConst \dm^\genConst \abs{\w_\dm \pr{x}}$ implies for all $\dm \in \N$, $x \in \R^\dm$, $\eps \in \err$, $a \in A$ that $\wdist_\dm \pr{ \tker_\dm^{\pr{a}} \pr{x, \cdot},  \tkerANN_{\dm, \eps}^{\pr{a}}\pr{x, \cdot} } \le \eps \genConst \dm^\genConst \abs{\w_\dm\pr{x}}$.
