    %
    in the notation of \cref{thm:main_simple})
    %
    %
    yields that there exists $c \in \R$ such that for every $\dm \in \N$, $\eps \in \err$ and every probability measure $\mu \colon \Borel\pr{\R^\dm} \to \br{0,1}$ with $\pr{\int_{\R^\dm} \abs{\w_\dm(x)}^2 \mu( \dxx x)}^{\nicefrac{1}{2}} \le \genConst d^\genConst$ it holds that
