\section{Related Work}

TOD systems have been extensively investigated in NLP. \cite{allen2001architecture}. 
% Early works in this area focused on rule-based approaches \cite{allen2001architecture}, where dialogue management strategies were predefined. With the advent of machine learning techniques, data-driven approaches gained prominence. 
Recent research has explored the use of neural network architectures for dialogue state tracking \cite{wu2020gcdst, zhao2021effective} and policy learning \cite{su2016line, liu2017iterative}.
% 
% Constraint-based dialogue systems leverage constraints to ensure the coherence and correctness of generated dialogues. Previous studies have proposed various constraint formalisms, including finite-state machines \cite{zhu2013robust}, hierarchical task networks \cite{georgievski2014overview}, and logical formalisms \cite{chen2004logic}. These systems aim to enforce constraints derived from domain knowledge and linguistic principles to enhance dialogue quality.
%The evaluation of dialogue systems is a crucial aspect of research in this domain. 
Several metrics have been proposed to assess the performance of TOD systems, including task completion rates, user satisfaction scores, and objective measures for system components, such as precision, recall, and F1-score \cite{chen2017survey, santhanam2019towards, deriu2021survey}. Recent studies have emphasized the importance of holistic evaluation frameworks that consider multiple aspects of dialogue quality \cite{zhang2021d}.

