A hierarchical MEC system that integrates HAPS and UAVs was proposed in \cite{10506092}. The authors formulated a task offloading problem that minimizes the long-term cost of processing tasks while considering  queuing during task offloading. To solve it, they proposed a multi-agent DRL-based computation algorithm, enhanced by a convolutional LSTM (ConvLSTM) for UAVs' task load estimation and a prioritized experience replay (PER) method to accelerate the model's convergence and training stability.
