We observe numerous references to human rights and foreign assistance on the edges of this subgraph. This is likely reflective of the US Congress' interest in the United Nations' involvement with these countries, e.g. investigating for human rights abuse and sending peacekeeping aid. In Africa, the United Nations Mission in the Sudan (UNMIS) was in place from 2005 to 2011 to gain stability in the hostile region, resulting in the formation of South Sudan \cite{un}. Meanwhile, in South America, the US government has investigated Colombia for "arbitrary or unlawful killings" and "serious restrictions on freedom of expression and media freedom" \cite{colombia}. Other clusters are similarly connected by their shared global interests and actions.
