a \emph{context} $\con$ is a set of variables and \emph{context set} $\cons$ is a downward closed set of contexts (i.e, $\con\in\cons$ and $\con
'\subseteq \con$ implies $\con'\in\cons$).  We often represent a context set \( \cons \) in terms of its maximal elements; for instance, we may write $\cons=\{\{x,y\},\{y,z\}\}$ to denote $\cons=\{\{x,y\},\{y,z\},\{x\},\{y\},\{z\},\emptyset\}$.  
