\begin{definition}[Contextual team semantics]
    Let $\mA$ be a finite $\tau$-structure and $\pX$ a contextual polyteam over $\cons$. The satisfaction relation $\models_\pX$ is defined inductively as follows:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item For atomic formulas $\phi$, $\mA \models_\pX \phi$ if $\mA \models_{\pX_\con}\phi$ for {all} $\con \in \cons$ such that $\Vars(\phi)\subseteq \con$.
       % \miika{Modified so as to accept when context does not contain all variables. See later PR box example.}
        \item $\mA \models_\pX \psi\land \theta$ if $\mA \models_\pX \psi$ and $\mA \models_\pX \theta$.
        \item $\mA \models_\pX \psi\lor \theta$ if $\mA \models_\pY \psi$ and $\mA \models_\pZ \theta$, for some $\pY$ and $\pZ$ such that $\pX = \pY+\pZ$. 
       % \item $\mA \models_\pX \psi\llor \theta$ if $\mA \models_{\pX_\con}\psi\lor \theta$ for {all} $\con \in \cons$ such that $\Vars(\psi\lor \theta)\subseteq \con$.
        \item $\mA \models_\pX \forall x\psi$ if $\mA \models_\pY \psi$, where $\pY$ is such that $\pY_\con(s[a/x])=\pX_\con(s)$ for all $\con \in \cons$, $s\in \as(\con, A)$ and $a\in A$.
        \item $\mA \models_\pX \exists x\psi$ if $\mA \models_\pY \psi$, for some $\pY$ such that
        $\sum_{a\in A} \pY_\con(s[a/x])=(\pX_\con \restr (C\setminus \{x\}))(s)$ for all $\con \in \cons$, $s\in \as(\con, A)$.
    \end{itemize}
    Note that $\pX_\con \restr (C\setminus \{x\})$ is simply $\pX_\con$ whenever $x$ does not belong to $C$.
    If the formula $\phi$ does not contain quantifiers or any functions or constant symbols from the vocabulary $\tau$, we may shorten the expression $\mA \models_\pX\phi$ as $\pX \models \phi$.
\end{definition}
If $\alpha$ is a first-order formula, we write $\alpha \to \phi$ as a shorthand for $\alpha^{\bot} \lor \phi$, where $\alpha^{\bot}$ is obtained from $\neg \alpha$ by pushing the negation in front of atomic formulas.

